We begin with a detailed overview of the intraday trend-following model used throughout the study and the main backtesting assumptions. We then introduce the ETF universe and the walk-forward ranking methodology used to select instruments each day. Finally, we assess whether past strategy performance can help distinguish future winners from losers. We also provide a detailed overview of the yearly performance of the strategy for each of the 49 ETFs, and discuss the main implications and possible extensions of the research.
